        "original_id": "b7d6b3d2-57c1-5c86-a6d5-dd0129acc329",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Bands: Red House Painters, Daughtry\n- People: Gorden Mack, Phil Carney, Chris Daughtry, Billy Anderson\n- Places: San Francisco, California\n- Albums: Republic?\n- Roles: producer, guitarist\n- Topics: band formation, band membership, production credits\n\nFacts:\n- Red House Painters were an American rock band formed in San Francisco, California in 1988.\n- Gorden Mack performed as a guitarist with Red House Painters during a six-year tenure.\n- Phil Carney performed as a guitarist with Red House Painters during a separate six-year tenure.\n- Daughtry is an American rock band formed and fronted by Chris Daughtry, who was a finalist on the fifth season of American Idol.\n- Over the past 29 years, Billy Anderson has worked with hundreds of bands, including Red House Painters, Neurosis, Swans, Melvins, Jawbreaker, Sleep, Brutal Truth, Buzzoven, Fantômas, Agalloch, Cattle Decapitation, Mr. Bungle, and Asunder.\n- Republic? was produced by Billy Anderson.",
